      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-145894",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Let the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$ be $F(x, y)$, where\n\n$F(6, 5) = \\frac{3}{5}, F(6, 3) = \\frac{2}{5}, F(6, 2) = \\frac{1}{10}$\n\nand the supports of $X$ and $Y$, respectively, are\n\n$S_{X} = {2, 6, 10}, S_{Y} = {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}$.\n\nFind $P(X < 7, Y > 3)$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
